s. The necessary investments for these differenciations are met by the relatively high prices that can be achieved - which usualy allows for very high margins.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offer targets a very select segment You can extract a lot of benefits from your beneficiaries that are very sensitive to quality or are looking for exclusive privileges.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"user_design\",\n      \"name\": \"User design\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Within user manufacturing, a customer is both the manufacturer and the customer. As an example, an online platform provides the customer with the necessary support in order to design and merchandise the product, e.g. product design software, manufacturing services, or an online shop to sell products. Thus, the company only supports the customers in their undertakings and benefits from their creativity. The customer benefits from the potential to realize entrepreneurial ideas without having to provide the required infrastructure. Revenue is then generated as part of the actual sales.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offer is to provide help entrepreneurs, to facilitate their work, even to source an enterprize (provide infrastructure, space, etc.), help with dissemination / distribution.  You benefit from the success of your beneficiaries (share of benefits agreement). Your beneficiaries are happy because they reduce their costs.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"ex. Sensorica, any incubator or accelerator.\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"white_label\",\n      \"name\": \"White Label\",\n      \"traditional\": \"A white label producer allows other companies to distribute its goods under their brands, so that it appears as if they are made by them. The same product or service is often sold by multiple marketers and under different brands. This way, various customer segments can be satisfied with the same product.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sensor_as_a_service\",\n      \"name\": \"Sensor as a Service\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The use of sensors permits additional services for physical offerings, or wholly new independent services. It is not the sensor that generates the primary revenue, but the analysis of the data that the sensor creates. Possibilities for real-time information can further strenghten the value proposition.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"visualization\",\n      \"name\": \"Visualization\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The pattern describes the imitation of a traditionally physical process in a virtual environment. E.g. a virtual workspace. The advantage for the customer is the ability to interact with the process from any location or device. In exchange, the customer pays for access to the virtual service.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your offer is a digital twin, a digital / virtual representation of a thing, a process, or both.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"object_self_service\",\n      \"name\": \"Object self-service\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Through the use of sensors and inclusion in an IT-structure, and object can generate orders itself. This makes fully automated processes like replenishment possible, and increases the speed of interaction with the object. The customer is locked in, giving rise to reccurent revenue.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"object_as_a_point_of_sale\",\n      \"name\": \"Object as a Point of Sale\",\n      \"traditional\": \"The point of sale of consumables moves to the point of consumption. This generates a stronger lock-in and results in higher customer retention. When the point of sale is shifted away from competing products, the customer becomes less sensitive to proce.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"The point of access of resources moves to the point of use. This generates a stronger confluence of peers and results in less possibility of design overlappings, not counting better usage of available resources. When the point of access is shifted away from collaborative designables the peer that seeks to develop new designs becomes less resourceful.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"prosumer\",\n      \"name\": \"Prosumer\",\n      \"traditional\": \"Companies enable the customer to become producers themselves. The customer is integrated into the value chain and can profit from resulting product, while the company has fewer investment costs for production and overhead. Since the customer has a hand in production, the perceived value of the product increases.\",\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Your beneficiaries become you peers and contribute to your innovation and production processes. Your organization is open. Your offering can better incorporate the needs of you beneficiaries, since they contribute to design your offer.\",\n      \"material_distributed\": \"\",\n      \"examples\": \"\",\n      \"dependability_measures\": \"\",\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"medium\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Keep contribution accounting and commons access; avoid enclosure of the shared layer; prefer transparency over opaque capture.\",\n      \"risks\": \"Capture via platform lock-in, brand enclosure, or capital-weighted governance.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"additional_ovn_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"commons_stewardship_as_a_service\",\n      \"name\": \"Commons Stewardship as a Service\",\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": [\n        \"S\",\n        \"O\",\n        \"E\"\n      ],\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Provide stewardship services for commons assets without claiming residual ownership.\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Custodian role separation; nondominium-compatible mandates.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"protocol_cooperative\",\n      \"name\": \"Protocol Cooperative\",\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": [\n        \"PL\",\n        \"E\",\n        \"MC\"\n      ],\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Cooperatively maintain protocols/interfaces that many ventures share.\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Open governance of protocol changes; infrastructure reciprocity.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"outcome_commons_contracting\",\n      \"name\": \"Outcome Commons Contracting\",\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": [\n        \"O\",\n        \"CM\"\n      ],\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Contract for shared outcomes while logging contributions to commons deliverables.\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Transparent outcome metrics; avoid privatizing the commons result.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"distributed_capability_incubation\",\n      \"name\": \"Distributed Capability Incubation\",\n      \"enterprise_stack_levels\": [\n        \"E\",\n        \"MC\"\n      ],\n      \"p2p_description\": \"Incubate capabilities across affiliates rather than concentrating IP in a single firm.\",\n      \"adaptation_rule\": \"Contribution-derived participation; portable reputation.\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"ovn_fit\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"}]